        "original_id": "0a06bc18-c26a-5944-bd3a-5a955fdc9ed9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Ilysiakos B.C.\n- People: Antonis Fotsis\n- Systems: Greek alphabet, Phoenician alphabet\n- Places: Ilissia, Elysium\n- Concepts: club name origin, Greek letters\n\nFacts:\n- The Greek alphabet was derived from the earlier Phoenician alphabet.\n- The Greek alphabet was the first alphabetic script to have distinct letters for both vowels and consonants.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name is said to reference Elysium.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name and logo begin with the Greek letter Η instead of Ι.\n- Ilissia, where Ilysiakos B.C. is based, begins with the Greek letter Ι.\n- Antonis Fotsis, also spelled Antonios, was born on April 2, 1981.\n- Antonis Fotsis is a Greek professional basketball player for Ilysiakos.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
